2025-05-01 03:04:03 - Thread-1175 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns, their possible usage, and conditions  

• event_date : identify the calendar day of every hit (convert with DATE(PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d',`event_date`))).  
  – Conditions: BETWEEN DATE '2018‑09‑01' AND DATE '2018‑09‑30'.  

• event_name : tells us which kind of hit it is.  
  – Conditions: = 'first_open' (first launch), = 'app_remove' (un‑install), = 'app_exception' (crash).  

• user_pseudo_id : anonymous user identifier – join / group on it.  

• event_timestamp : micro‑seconds since epoch – can be used instead of event_date when we really need exact time.  
  – TIMESTAMP_MICROS(event_timestamp) to obtain a TIMESTAMP.  

• _TABLE_SUFFIX (virtual column when a wildcard is used) : lets us restrict queries to all daily tables that belong to September 2018 ( `'20180901' … '20180930'`).  

---------------------------------------------------------------------------  
Ten exploratory → final BigQuery queries (each returns ≤20 rows, each different).  

```sql
--1. Description: show the distinct event names that exist in the table of 1‑Sep‑2018.
